  <data name="dev_section_title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>For developers</value>
  </data>
  <data name="dev_web_mobile_title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Web-Mobile applications</value>
  </data>
  <data name="dev_web_mobile_desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Web-Mobile applications are games and educational apps developed using web technologies (HTML5, CSS, JavaScript) optimized for mobile devices in a browser. They provide cross-platform access and do not require installation.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="dev_instructions_title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Instructions for developers</value>
  </data>
  <data name="dev_guide_step_1_title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>1. Application preparation</value>
  </data>
  <data name="dev_guide_step_1_desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Build an app using HTML5, CSS, and JavaScript. Make sure it is responsive across screen sizes (320px to 768px). Use frameworks such as Phaser for games or React for interactive apps.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="dev_guide_step_2_title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>2. Testing</value>
  </data>
  <data name="dev_guide_step_2_desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Test the application in popular mobile browsers (Chrome, Safari, Firefox). Ensure it meets WCAG 2.1 accessibility standards. Check performance using tools like Lighthouse.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="dev_guide_step_3_title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>3. Metadata preparation</value>
  </data>
  <data name="dev_guide_step_3_desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Create an appealing cover (recommended size: 294x424px), prepare screenshots and description. Specify categories (e.g., "Vocabulary", "Grammar") and keywords for search.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="dev_guide_step_4_title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>4. Publishing</value>
  </data>
  <data name="dev_guide_step_4_desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Upload the application using the form on the Upload Game page. Provide the game URL or upload a ZIP archive. After moderator approval, the app will appear under "Recommended Games".</value>
  </data>
  <data name="dev_web_desktop_title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Web-Desktop applications</value>
  </data>
  <data name="dev_web_desktop_desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Web-Desktop applications are web apps optimized for desktop browsers. They are suited for more complex educational games requiring larger screens and performance.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="dev_web_desktop_guide_step_1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Develop the application using HTML5, CSS, and JavaScript. Canvas or WebGL is recommended for complex visual effects. Ensure the UI is comfortable for mouse and keyboard use.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="dev_web_desktop_guide_step_2" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Test the app in Chrome, Firefox, and Edge. Optimize performance for screens from 1280x720px resolution. Use tools like Chrome DevTools for debugging.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="dev_web_desktop_guide_step_3" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Prepare a cover (294x424px), screenshots, and detailed description. Specify difficulty level (e.g., "Young Nart" or "Caucasian Eagle") and categories.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="dev_web_desktop_guide_step_4" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Upload the application via the form on the Upload Game page. Provide a URL or ZIP archive. After review, the application will appear in the catalog.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="dev_desktop_apps_title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Desktop applications</value>
  </data>
  <data name="dev_desktop_apps_desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Desktop applications are standalone programs for Windows, macOS, or Linux that users download and install. They suit complex educational applications with high interactivity.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="dev_desktop_guide_step_1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Develop the application using a suitable language (e.g., C++, Python with Pygame, or Unity). Ensure support for popular operating systems (Windows, macOS, Linux).</value>
  </data>
  <data name="dev_desktop_guide_step_2" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Test the application on target platforms. Ensure it has no errors and meets security requirements. Check the installer package (EXE, DMG, or AppImage).</value>
  </data>
  <data name="dev_desktop_guide_step_3" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Create a cover (294x424px), screenshots, and description. Specify system requirements and supported operating systems.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="dev_desktop_guide_step_4" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Upload the installer file (ZIP, RAR, APK, EXE, DMG) via the form on the Upload Game page. After verification, the application will be available for download.</value>
  </data>
